target/
# Build output of `breath`. Written by the two-step build documented in
# AGENTS.md — `wasm-bindgen` writes the two wasm artefacts into `dist/`, then
# `build.rs` publishes the rest of the site — and reproducible from the
# committed sources. Never committed: a committed build is a build that rots
# silently, shipping a pacer that predates the code that produced it.
dist/

# Release recovery journals. They live inside the repository so a read-only
# copy root cannot stop a release recording itself, and they are archived rather
# than deleted, so the directory persists after a successful release. Without
# this, every release leaves master permanently "dirty": the untracked directory
# changes nothing a reviewer would look at, so it is easy to sweep into a commit
# with `git add -A` and to mistake for a real working change. It has never been
# committed here, but it is not a thing to rely on noticing.
.release-recovery/
